WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:01.935 align:start size:94% position:6%
-"The Orville."

00:00:01.935 --> 00:00:03.937 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, uh, takes place
400 years in the future.

00:00:03.937 --> 00:00:05.505 align:start size:94% position:6%
Tell us a little bit.
-It does.

00:00:05.505 --> 00:00:10.276 align:start size:94% position:6%
It is an hour-long
sci-fi comedic drama

00:00:10.276 --> 00:00:11.978 align:start size:94% position:6%
is the best way to put it.
-Yeah.

00:00:11.978 --> 00:00:13.513
-We kind of straddle a line

00:00:13.513 --> 00:00:15.882 align:start size:94% position:6%
between comedy
and legit science-fiction.

00:00:15.882 --> 00:00:17.117 align:start size:94% position:6%
We´re kind of
trying something new here.

00:00:17.117 --> 00:00:19.285 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And it´s an hour,
and there are --

00:00:19.285 --> 00:00:21.421 align:start size:94% position:6%
There´s an actual story
and a plot.

00:00:21.421 --> 00:00:22.722 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-It´s not --

00:00:22.722 --> 00:00:24.224
You know, it´s not just --

00:00:24.224 --> 00:00:27.460
Based on your other work,
it´s not just a series of jokes

00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:29.929 align:start size:94% position:6%
that are, like,
followed for the laugh.

00:00:29.929 --> 00:00:33.033 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. In 30 minutes,
we could make it a sitcom,

00:00:33.033 --> 00:00:35.535 align:start size:94% position:6%
but with an hour,
you know, again, it´s --

00:00:35.535 --> 00:00:37.871 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is something that
hasn´t really been attempted,

00:00:37.871 --> 00:00:40.640 align:start size:94% position:6%
and we think we´ve kind of
cracked the code.

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:42.108 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Is it an idea
you´ve had for a long time?

00:00:42.108 --> 00:00:43.410 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, yeah.

00:00:43.410 --> 00:00:44.944
Look, I´ve always been obviously
a big fan of comedy --

00:00:44.944 --> 00:00:45.945 size:78% position:39%
I worked in comedy --

00:00:45.945 --> 00:00:47.947 align:start size:94% position:6%
but I was always
a big sci-fi fan

00:00:47.947 --> 00:00:50.016 size:81% position:41%
and had never really
written in that genre,

00:00:50.016 --> 00:00:54.421 align:start size:94% position:6%
and, you know,
it´s always a tough sell

00:00:54.421 --> 00:00:55.789 align:start size:94% position:6%
to kind of combine
these two things.

00:00:55.789 --> 00:00:57.223 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.

00:00:57.223 --> 00:00:59.492
-You know, recently, with things
like "Guardians of the Galaxy"

00:00:59.492 --> 00:01:01.461 size:81% position:41%
and "Deadpool," like,
audiences kind of seem

00:01:01.461 --> 00:01:03.830
a little bit more willing
to kind of accept that marriage.

00:01:03.830 --> 00:01:06.733 align:start size:94% position:6%
And no one´s
ever really tried it for TV

00:01:06.733 --> 00:01:08.401 size:84% position:42%
in an hour-long format.

00:01:08.401 --> 00:01:10.336 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I said, "What the hell?"
you know?

00:01:10.336 --> 00:01:12.005 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-"Fox, what do you think?"

00:01:12.005 --> 00:01:15.175
-Fox owes you nothing but money.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:15.175 --> 00:01:16.776 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And, you know,
it´s a big swing,

00:01:16.776 --> 00:01:17.944
and we´ll see if it goes,

00:01:17.944 --> 00:01:19.846 align:start size:94% position:6%
but we feel like
we got something special.

00:01:19.846 --> 00:01:22.682 size:84% position:42%
-So, I think, you know,
an example of something

00:01:22.682 --> 00:01:25.752 align:start size:94% position:6%
that is both comic
but also character-driven

00:01:25.752 --> 00:01:29.089 align:start size:94% position:6%
that leads to story
is your co-captain

00:01:29.089 --> 00:01:31.057 align:start size:94% position:6%
is your ex-wife.
-Yes.

00:01:31.057 --> 00:01:32.759
-Is that something
you sort of realized right away

00:01:32.759 --> 00:01:34.194 align:start size:94% position:6%
you wanted to have
be an element of this?

00:01:34.194 --> 00:01:35.762 size:81% position:41%
-Yeah, it felt like --

00:01:35.762 --> 00:01:38.164
You know, the best sci-fi for me
is the stuff

00:01:38.164 --> 00:01:40.767 align:start size:94% position:6%
that kind of casualizes
the world and humanizes it,

00:01:40.767 --> 00:01:43.236 size:84% position:42%
makes it oddly mundane.

00:01:43.236 --> 00:01:45.839
A lot of sci-fi tends to be
very operatic and very big.

00:01:45.839 --> 00:01:48.341
And, yeah, that just
seemed like something that was,

00:01:48.341 --> 00:01:50.376 align:start size:94% position:6%
you put the captain
and his first officer,

00:01:50.376 --> 00:01:52.445 align:start size:94% position:6%
who´s his ex-wife,
side by side every week,

00:01:52.445 --> 00:01:54.247 size:81% position:41%
you´re never gonna --
you´re never gonna get

00:01:54.247 --> 00:01:55.682
too out of the realm of reality,

00:01:55.682 --> 00:01:57.884
because you´re always gonna have
that staring you in the face.

00:01:57.884 --> 00:01:59.185 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-And, of course, you know,

00:01:59.185 --> 00:02:00.954
we have Adrianne Palicki,
from "Friday Night Lights,"

00:02:00.954 --> 00:02:02.522 align:start size:94% position:6%
who´s brilliant.
-Fantastic actress.

00:02:02.522 --> 00:02:03.857 align:start size:94% position:6%
-She´s amazing.
-Yeah.

00:02:03.857 --> 00:02:06.493 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it´s -- it´s --
I -- I --

00:02:06.493 --> 00:02:08.495
It´s different, and I think
it´s gonna surprise people

00:02:08.495 --> 00:02:09.529
but hopefully in a good way.

00:02:09.529 --> 00:02:11.664
-You have some amazing cameos --

00:02:11.664 --> 00:02:15.068 align:start size:94% position:6%
Jeffrey Tambor,
Charlize is in it.

00:02:15.068 --> 00:02:19.005
But you -- brilliant use of
the legendary Norm Macdonald.

00:02:19.005 --> 00:02:22.008
Because if you´re gonna have
Norm Macdonald on a sci-fi show,

00:02:22.008 --> 00:02:23.877 align:start size:94% position:6%
feels like
you have a lot of options.

00:02:23.877 --> 00:02:25.812 align:start size:94% position:6%
Tell us what you went with
and how you got there.

00:02:25.812 --> 00:02:28.414 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know,
he plays a gelatinous blob...

00:02:28.414 --> 00:02:31.818 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:31.818 --> 00:02:33.820 align:start size:94% position:6%
...named Yaphit...
-Yeah.

00:02:33.820 --> 00:02:36.222 align:start size:94% position:6%
-...which looks good on paper,
but then when you realize

00:02:36.222 --> 00:02:38.424 align:start size:94% position:6%
you have to do
a CGI character every week,

00:02:38.424 --> 00:02:40.793 align:start size:94% position:6%
it starts
to become very expensive,

00:02:40.793 --> 00:02:42.595 align:start size:94% position:6%
and so you maybe
write him back a little bit.

00:02:42.595 --> 00:02:43.930 align:start size:94% position:6%
But he´s hilarious.

00:02:43.930 --> 00:02:46.499 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I called him, I said,
"Norm, you want to be a blob?"

00:02:46.499 --> 00:02:48.067 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:48.067 --> 00:02:49.969 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Like, "Yeah, yeah, yeah,
I´ll be a blob, sure.

00:02:49.969 --> 00:02:51.437 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:51.437 --> 00:02:54.107
And then, you know, he´s one of
the funniest guys out there.

00:02:54.107 --> 00:02:57.310
-He is the funniest guy out
there, and it´s really fun.

00:02:57.310 --> 00:03:00.413
You realize, to hear his voice,

00:03:00.413 --> 00:03:03.049 align:start size:94% position:6%
you are immediately,
the blob is Norm.

00:03:03.049 --> 00:03:04.651 size:88% position:44%
-Yeah, exactly, exactly.

00:03:04.651 --> 00:03:06.085
Which the thing has no face,

00:03:06.085 --> 00:03:07.353 align:start size:94% position:6%
so it had
to be something that --

00:03:07.353 --> 00:03:09.522
-Yeah it´s just a mouth.
-All had to come from the voice.

00:03:09.522 --> 00:03:12.192
-And obviously, it´s very hard,
very time-intensive to you.

00:03:12.192 --> 00:03:13.860 align:start size:94% position:6%
It seems like Norm´s
got the best job on Earth.

00:03:13.860 --> 00:03:15.361 align:start size:94% position:6%
What is he doing,
Like 20 minutes a week?

00:03:15.361 --> 00:03:16.996 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, yeah, he´s set.
He´s set.

00:03:16.996 --> 00:03:18.831 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-But it´s a golden 20 minutes.

00:03:18.831 --> 00:03:21.134
-Yeah, it´s a golden 20 minutes.
I feel like he´s figured it out.

00:03:21.134 --> 00:03:24.270 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I want to ask about your
album, "In Full Swing."

00:03:24.270 --> 00:03:26.039
So, was this exciting to do?

00:03:26.039 --> 00:03:28.708
-Yeah, this was --
These things are always a blast.

00:03:28.708 --> 00:03:31.444
This is my other side gig.

00:03:31.444 --> 00:03:35.248 align:start size:94% position:6%
We recorded this
at Abbey Road, in London,

00:03:35.248 --> 00:03:37.650 align:start size:94% position:6%
with about
a 40-, 45-piece orchestra.

00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:39.219 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Wow.

00:03:39.219 --> 00:03:43.022
-Joel McNeely, who actually
does scoring for "Orville,"

00:03:43.022 --> 00:03:44.190
did all the arrangements.

00:03:44.190 --> 00:03:46.492 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it´s --
You know, this is --

00:03:46.492 --> 00:03:49.596 align:start size:94% position:6%
It´s all big-band swing tunes
with strings.

00:03:49.596 --> 00:03:52.799 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And how long --
how intensive, time-wise,

00:03:52.799 --> 00:03:55.401 align:start size:94% position:6%
is that process to do an album
with that many musicians?

00:03:55.401 --> 00:03:57.370 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It´s -- It´s...

00:03:57.370 --> 00:03:58.738
Because it´s all kind of --

00:03:58.738 --> 00:04:00.640 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, we do as much of it
live as we can.

00:04:00.640 --> 00:04:04.244
You´re in there with the
musicians like they used to do.

00:04:04.244 --> 00:04:05.411 align:start size:94% position:6%
It´s not --

00:04:05.411 --> 00:04:06.746 size:78% position:39%
The production itself
is like three days.

00:04:06.746 --> 00:04:07.981 align:start size:94% position:6%
You record the whole thing
in three days.

00:04:07.981 --> 00:04:09.048 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, wow.

00:04:09.048 --> 00:04:10.817 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Because you´re there,
the band´s there,

00:04:10.817 --> 00:04:13.786
and what´s in the room is
what winds up in the recording.

00:04:13.786 --> 00:04:16.623 align:start size:94% position:6%
-In the lead up,
how hard is it for you

00:04:16.623 --> 00:04:17.924
to actually select down to --

00:04:17.924 --> 00:04:19.892 align:start size:94% position:6%
What are you -- 16, 20 songs?
Like, around...?

00:04:19.892 --> 00:04:21.327 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Like, is that --

00:04:21.327 --> 00:04:23.963 align:start size:94% position:6%
Do you kind of know for years
the ones you want to do?

00:04:23.963 --> 00:04:25.565 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know,
I have a long list of things

00:04:25.565 --> 00:04:26.866
I´d eventually like to do.

00:04:26.866 --> 00:04:30.803 align:start size:94% position:6%
For these kinds of records,
you can´t really --

00:04:30.803 --> 00:04:32.772 size:81% position:41%
Because you´re dealing
with so many musicians

00:04:32.772 --> 00:04:34.040
and the time and the cost,

00:04:34.040 --> 00:04:36.009 align:start size:94% position:6%
you really do have
to narrow it down beforehand.

00:04:36.009 --> 00:04:37.977 align:start size:94% position:6%
So we picked,
"All right, these 15 or 16,

00:04:37.977 --> 00:04:40.380
and this is what´s gonna be
on the record, no cuts."

00:04:40.380 --> 00:04:42.382
-Do you think that janitor
ever hears this album and goes,

00:04:42.382 --> 00:04:43.783 align:start size:94% position:6%
"That´s my voice"?

00:04:43.783 --> 00:04:45.385 size:78% position:39%
-it´s possible, yeah.

00:04:45.385 --> 00:04:47.687
-Do people -- Do you know
that people resent you

00:04:47.687 --> 00:04:49.022
because you can sing
and do a lot of other things...

00:04:49.022 --> 00:04:50.356 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Is that right?

00:04:50.356 --> 00:04:51.591 align:start size:94% position:6%
-...and it feels like
you should only be able to do

00:04:51.591 --> 00:04:52.725 size:88% position:44%
like one or two of them?

00:04:52.725 --> 00:04:53.860 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Man...

00:04:53.860 --> 00:04:55.261 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And then it´s like
you kind of can sing

00:04:55.261 --> 00:04:56.529 align:start size:94% position:6%
and write and draw and act?
-That´s why the critics

00:04:56.529 --> 00:04:57.563 align:start size:94% position:6%
are always beating
the [bleep] out of me.

00:04:57.563 --> 00:04:58.831 size:81% position:41%
-Yeah, they´re like --

00:04:58.831 --> 00:05:01.501 align:start size:94% position:6%
They´re kind of like,
"Pick your lane, buddy."

00:05:01.501 --> 00:05:03.503 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Grinding the axe.

00:05:03.503 --> 00:05:04.704 size:88% position:44%
-With that said, though,

00:05:04.704 --> 00:05:06.439 align:start size:94% position:6%
you obviously,
as we´ve discussed,

00:05:06.439 --> 00:05:09.175
you´ve made fun of people,
you´ve made fun of celebrities.

00:05:09.175 --> 00:05:11.611 align:start size:94% position:6%
It does seem like
people end up --

00:05:11.611 --> 00:05:13.246 align:start size:94% position:6%
you end up getting cameos
on your show.

00:05:13.246 --> 00:05:14.380
Have you ever had a situation

00:05:14.380 --> 00:05:16.215
where you´ve
reached out to somebody and say,

00:05:16.215 --> 00:05:17.684 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Hey, you´d be perfect
for this,"

00:05:17.684 --> 00:05:19.819 align:start size:94% position:6%
and they said, "Hey, actually,
I´m not gonna do that,

00:05:19.819 --> 00:05:21.754
because you did this to me"?

00:05:21.754 --> 00:05:23.423 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That´s a --
Not that I can think of.

00:05:23.423 --> 00:05:25.158 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Gotcha.
-That´s a very good question.

00:05:25.158 --> 00:05:28.461 align:start size:94% position:6%
No. I mean,
we´ve had people who have --

00:05:28.461 --> 00:05:30.196 size:75% position:38%
Usually what happens
is the other thing,

00:05:30.196 --> 00:05:32.565 align:start size:94% position:6%
where we´ll take a shot at
somebody and we´ll think that,

00:05:32.565 --> 00:05:34.400
you know,
"They´re gonna hate us for this.

00:05:34.400 --> 00:05:37.270
And then we´ll run into the
person or they´ll call and say,

00:05:37.270 --> 00:05:38.504 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Hey, I love that thing on
´Family Guy.´

00:05:38.504 --> 00:05:40.106
Can I come in and do the show?"
-Oh, wow.

00:05:40.106 --> 00:05:42.041 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And then we´re obligated to,
you know...

00:05:42.041 --> 00:05:43.343 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right.
Yeah, exactly.

00:05:43.343 --> 00:05:44.844 size:78% position:39%
-There was a great --

00:05:44.844 --> 00:05:46.713
It was a great moment where

00:05:46.713 --> 00:05:48.948 align:start size:94% position:6%
Peter Griffin
took a shot at Cary Elwes.

00:05:48.948 --> 00:05:50.850 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Uh-huh.
What a weird shot to take.

00:05:50.850 --> 00:05:52.018 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:05:52.018 --> 00:05:54.053 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Cary Elwes, "Princess Bride",
fantastic actor.

00:05:54.053 --> 00:05:57.690
-But he´s writing kind of
a fan letter to Cary Elwes

00:05:57.690 --> 00:06:00.827 align:start size:94% position:6%
that´s full of, you know,
a couple of jabs,

00:06:00.827 --> 00:06:02.929
and one day in the writers room,
Cary Elwes just walks in...

00:06:02.929 --> 00:06:04.163 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, my God.

00:06:04.163 --> 00:06:05.932 align:start size:94% position:6%
-...and reads the response
that he had written.

00:06:05.932 --> 00:06:06.966 size:81% position:41%
-Oh, that´s fantastic.

00:06:06.966 --> 00:06:08.668 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Now he´s like
our friend for life.

00:06:08.668 --> 00:06:10.203 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:06:10.203 --> 00:06:11.838 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You have terrible security.
-I know!

00:06:11.838 --> 00:06:12.905 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:06:12.905 --> 00:06:15.375
If Cary Elwes can just walk in

00:06:15.375 --> 00:06:17.143 align:start size:94% position:6%
to a television production,
what´s next?

00:06:17.143 --> 00:06:18.277 size:88% position:44%
-Well, that´s fantastic.

00:06:18.277 --> 00:06:19.545 align:start size:94% position:6%
I´m so happy to hear
what a good sport he is.

00:06:19.545 --> 00:06:20.913 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, he´s awesome.
-And thanks for being here.

00:06:20.913 --> 00:06:22.215 align:start size:94% position:6%
Congrats on the new show
and everything else.

00:06:22.215 --> 00:06:24.016 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thanks so much, man.
-Always good to see you.

00:06:24.016 --> 00:06:25.184
Seth MacFarlane, everybody.

